{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${y}_{0}=1$ and ${y}_{n}=5$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{i} & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122984/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122984"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122986/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d5015149-a7c0-56d4-bea9-484e8e219668" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122986/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "9216941a-8885-56de-a118-ed0661b7976e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122986/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "036ee26e-6baa-5149-ac14-1072e00e664a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122986/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "30e87b29-7877-5984-bef9-163aa0126013" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122986/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "015befc4-0e54-5cda-88fd-b8e9948551b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122986/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fba39ec4-264f-5106-b61b-3f4facd9e979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122986/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-122986/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-122986/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-122986/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-122986/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-122986/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122986" :question/id #uuid "e927f605-c6c3-53fd-b804-31aa5274ceef" :question/math-academy-id "q-122986" :question/problem "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[-2,2].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=-2$ and ${z}_{q}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-(-2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122986/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122986"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-122849"] :question/problem "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,2].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=0$ and ${x}_{m}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-122992/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer/id #uuid "6b42bb14-69ce-5638-9395-6c34c6096d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122992/selection/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" :answer/id #uuid "84a27534-8b82-59a6-b35e-0f81bea16700" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122992/selection/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" :answer/id #uuid "080b9100-4cb3-583b-a0c1-ebf86a00ebc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122992/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "f214d946-2e1e-59ca-83f6-0314b9cbe194" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122992/selection/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e" :answer/id #uuid "92832543-05fb-5129-a7aa-e8c8027ec596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122992/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f1c01ac7-9d26-51e2-9d1e-e1b4c6519d81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122992/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" :answer-field/choices ["q-122992/selection/594f4371237f716a4e7b771cfac6a2ca8b8eb3c8dcb7752f2b3291728275476a" "q-122992/selection/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" "q-122992/selection/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" "q-122992/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-122992/selection/5d34995cddd0166b343cae457ee45643c04c739e08758db1204c66c5ee04158e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122992" :question/id #uuid "061c82af-1f52-5108-8d09-031ae4712e6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122992" :question/problem "Let $P={{z}_{0},{z}_{1},…,{z}_{q}}$ be a partition of the interval $[-2,4].$ If $Δ{z}_{k}={z}_{k}-{z}_{k-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}-2({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}-2({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=-2{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}.\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the summation as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})Δ{z}_{1}+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})Δ{z}_{2}+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})Δ{z}_{n} \\\\  & =({z}_{1}+{z}_{0})({z}_{1}-{z}_{0})+({z}_{2}+{z}_{1})({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})+⋯+({z}_{q}+{z}_{q-1})({z}_{q}-{z}_{q-1}) \\\\  & =({z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2})+({z}_{2}^{2}-{z}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{q-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}}-{z}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{z}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{z}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({z}_{q}^{2}-\\cancel{{z}_{q-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{z}_{0}^{2}+{z}_{q}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${z}_{0}=-2$ and ${z}_{q}=4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k} & ={z}_{q}^{2}-{z}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-2)^{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{k=1}^{q}({z}_{k}+{z}_{k-1})Δ{z}_{k}=(-2)\\cdot 12=-24.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122992/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122992"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122988/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" :answer/id #uuid "6184aae7-d5b6-539e-8c4c-d9ae0deed07d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122988/selection/57a3ae1161af9413554a1cb9218656e1f4442c31b5d01877864c58878ea984a5" :answer/id #uuid "fb55434d-11c9-579a-9b03-0b80878466f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "78" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122988/selection/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" :answer/id #uuid "0a517e33-27c8-537b-b554-b0829344fc79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122988/selection/0fcb2bb891929980a55765997d5489abfc663cf792cecb9464e97759b6cc7a6f" :answer/id #uuid "a5d3b5c1-8d43-513b-a7bd-ca67ea5212d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "74" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122988/selection/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer/id #uuid "f1dbee7c-d030-5239-8654-6b28a7a3f8db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122988/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b00dc8cc-47bd-5abb-ae0d-f268b7b2b1f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122988/selection/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a" :answer-field/choices ["q-122988/selection/bdda2450817a39aa33f63c44268d508ac25aa607d31de284a7a3098288a61525" "q-122988/selection/57a3ae1161af9413554a1cb9218656e1f4442c31b5d01877864c58878ea984a5" "q-122988/selection/0086db6077a62a5e2d9c771f7cdf57bea92b1de496b4d9b1d9c50dc1e5b58991" "q-122988/selection/0fcb2bb891929980a55765997d5489abfc663cf792cecb9464e97759b6cc7a6f" "q-122988/selection/eb57fb392c21478621c4c209554229c785123f38918aca582a228a144fdce87a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122988" :question/id #uuid "9c5d330c-99be-5865-a9b7-c02497b1387b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122988" :question/problem "Let $P={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}}$ be a partition of the interval $[5,10].$ If $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${y}_{0}=5$ and ${y}_{n}=10$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{i} & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={10}^{2}-{5}^{2} \\\\  & =75.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-122988/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f55bdc9-4066-5786-bafe-c3fdc96a06c9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122988"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9484"] :question/problem "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]?$\n\n- $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n\n- $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n\n- $1 <     2  <    9$" :question/worked-solution "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9480"] :question/problem "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =Δ{y}_{1}+Δ{y}_{2}+Δ{y}_{3}+⋯+Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9481"] :question/problem "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$" :question/worked-solution "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
